  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/FarhanLodi/EasyOcrSharp",
  "published": "2026-11-15T05:34:21.63Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "3.2.0: Tracks EasyOcrSharp 3.2.0 (EasyImageSharp 1.2.0, ONNX Runtime 1.31.1, the PaddleOcrNet 2.4.0 structure engine). New flags on scan and pdf: --engine easyocr|ppocrv5 selects the recognition engine, --text-layer ignore|prefer|auto reads born-digital PDF pages from their embedded text, and --dpi auto (or 0, previously rejected) sizes each PDF page to the detector. Deskewed output now reports boxes on the input image. No other command, flag, output format or exit code changed. 3.1.1: Tracks EasyOcrSharp 3.1.1 (EasyImageSharp 1.1.0, ONNX Runtime 1.30.0, the PaddleOcrNet 2.1.0 structure engine, the GPU runtime deployment fix and the line-grouping fix). info, scan and pdf now report the execution provider that actually ran rather than the first non-CPU provider listed. No command, flag or exit code changed. 3.1.0: Tracks EasyOcrSharp 3.1.0, which adds tagged OpenTelemetry metrics (recorded on failures too, not just successes), opt-in concurrency limiting and per-operation timeouts, a warm-up hosted service, and a health check that verifies OCR actually runs rather than only that model files exist. No command, flag, output format or exit code changed. 3.0.0: Tracks EasyOcrSharp 3.0.0. The imaging stack moves to EasyImageSharp and the PP-StructureV3 document-structure engine is now built into EasyOcrSharp rather than coming from the third-party PaddleOcrNet package, so no split-licensed dependency remains anywhere in the graph. Models are served from the EasyOcrSharp model repository and cached in one directory shared with the library (%LOCALAPPDATA%/EasyOcrSharp/models), so structure models re-download once after upgrading. No command, flag, output format or exit code changed.",
